### BLOCKERS — this attempt is REJECTED until every one is resolved
- [blocker] The provider calls ContentstackLivePreview.init({ enable: true, ssr: true, mode: 'preview' }) unconditionally on every page load for every user, including production where CONTENTSTACK_LIVE_PREVIEW is not 'true'. This directly contradicts the component's own doc comment ('intentionally a no-op ... when CONTENTSTACK_LIVE_PREVIEW is not enabled') and runs the third-party preview SDK (script injection, postMessage listeners) in production. The diff already computes and exports isLivePreviewEnabled from src/services/contentstack.ts, but the provider never consumes it. (src/components/LivePreview/LivePreviewProvider.tsx:55)
  - Suggested fix: Import isLivePreviewEnabled from 'services/contentstack' and bail out of the useEffect early when it is false (if (!isLivePreviewEnabled || typeof window === 'undefined') return;), and pass enable: isLivePreviewEnabled to init. This makes the code match its documented contract.
### Advisory — apply where it makes the change smaller or clearer
- [major] Two empty stray artifacts (jest_out.txt, jest_out2.txt, both 0 bytes) are added at the repo root — accidental debug output from a local test run. They must not be merged. (jest_out.txt)
  - Suggested fix: Delete jest_out.txt and jest_out2.txt from the commit (git rm), and consider adding them to .gitignore if this pattern recurs.
- [minor] useLivePreviewEntryChange is exported from src/hooks/index.ts but has no production consumer anywhere in src/ (grep for 'useLivePreviewEntryChange' finds only the hook and its spec). It is currently dead scaffolding; the actual refresh behaviour is implemented via router.replace in LivePreviewProvider. (src/hooks/useLivePreview.ts:17)
  - Suggested fix: Either wire the hook into a real consumer in this story, or defer adding it (and its barrel export) to the follow-up story that consumes it, keeping this diff to the provider + stack config.
- [minor] The OnEntryChangeCallback type is declared locally and duplicated verbatim in src/hooks/useLivePreview.ts. Two copies of the same SDK-compat type will drift. (src/components/LivePreview/LivePreviewProvider.tsx:6)
  - Suggested fix: Declare the type once (e.g. in src/hooks/useLivePreview.ts or a shared types file) and import it in LivePreviewProvider.
- [minor] router.replace appends ?ts=<epoch> to the visible URL permanently on every entry-change event. Pages that read router.query will now see a spurious 'ts' param, and the timestamp accumulates in the address bar/history. (src/components/LivePreview/LivePreviewProvider.tsx:42)
  - Suggested fix: Prefer router.reload() (Next.js re-fetches getServerSideProps/getStaticProps without mutating the URL), or strip the ts param after navigation if cache-busting is genuinely required.



